From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:12:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] x87: C1 says whether a result was rounded up

x86 sets C1 after an arithmetic instruction, a store, a conversion to an
integer or a transcendental when rounding increased the result's
magnitude, and clears it otherwise; FPTAN reports the tangent's rounding
and FSINCOS the cosine's. An embedding host that runs x86 programs
exactly needs it.

SoftFloat's rounding routines for extended, single and double results,
for conversions to an integer and for extF80_roundToInt now raise a new,
non-exception flag, softfloat_flag_roundedUp, when the rounded magnitude
exceeds the truncated one, an overflow to infinity included. The x87
helpers copy it into C1, which an invalid operation, an unmasked
denormal operand or division by zero, and a store an unmasked overflow
or underflow keeps from memory clear instead.
